From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8150: keep CPUSS RBCPR clock critical

The production clk_summary shows gcc_cpuss_rbcpr_clk enabled in hardware
with no Linux consumer.  It is the only unmarked CPUSS-related gate in that
set; gcc_cpuss_dvm_bus_clk and gcc_cpuss_gnoc_clk are already critical.

This is an unverified candidate for the observed failure when
clk_ignore_unused is removed.  It must not be treated as a fix until the
candidate boots on the handset without the command-line safety flag.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8150.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8150.c
@@ -1379,6 +1379,7 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_cpuss_rbcpr_clk = {
 		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
 		.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 			.name = "gcc_cpuss_rbcpr_clk",
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
 		},
 	},
